84
00:07:10.599 --> 00:07:17.130
NARRATOR: On screen, compare two side-by-side
data structures, highlighting operation costs

85
00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:24.255
and invariant constraints for each, with a
decision flowchart guiding the choice.

86
00:07:24.255 --> 00:07:29.946
NARRATOR: Locate the first point where
observed behavior diverges from expected

87
00:07:29.946 --> 00:07:33.568
behavior, then test the smallest plausible
cause.

88
00:07:33.568 --> 00:07:40.030
NARRATOR: The diagnosis is strongest when
another person can reproduce the observation

89
00:07:40.030 --> 00:07:41.646
and the test.

90
00:07:41.762 --> 00:07:48.176
NARRATOR: Connect Algorithm Design Process to
the earlier ideas and explain how the pieces

91
00:07:48.176 --> 00:07:50.008
work as one system.

92
00:07:50.008 --> 00:07:56.559
NARRATOR: A disciplined solution states inputs
and outputs, proves correctness, and then

93
00:07:56.559 --> 00:07:58.743
analyzes time and space.

94
00:07:58.743 --> 00:08:06.959
NARRATOR: Consider this worked case: Before
coding, a developer specifies the input array

95
00:08:06.959 --> 00:08:14.544
and expected sorted output, verifies
correctness via trace, and calculates O(n log

96
00:08:14.544 --> 00:08:18.336
n) time and O(n) space requirements.

97
00:08:18.336 --> 00:08:25.953
NARRATOR: On screen, show a three-step
workflow diagram: Input/Output specification

98
00:08:25.953 --> 00:08:33.571
